268
00:16:58,080 --> 00:16:58,660
Yoo-hoo!

269
00:16:58,660 --> 00:17:02,940
Nezuko, please let go of my sword!

270
00:17:03,120 --> 00:17:03,540
Nezuko!

271
00:17:03,540 --> 00:17:03,720
Nezuko!

272
00:17:09,720 --> 00:17:15,140
She's set it ablaze, using her blood!

273
00:17:16,720 --> 00:17:18,720
The sword's changing color!

274
00:17:18,720 --> 00:17:24,220
The temperature's rising, causing my black sword to turn red!

275
00:17:24,220 --> 00:17:27,080
Shrouded in exploding blood!

276
00:17:27,680 --> 00:17:28,680
This is...

277
00:17:28,680 --> 00:17:33,840
Exploding blood sword!

278
00:17:33,840 --> 00:17:37,540
So it turns red, right?

279
00:17:38,300 --> 00:17:43,160
Mr. Samurai, your sword turns red only during the heat of battle, isn't that right?

280
00:17:43,880 --> 00:17:44,700
What is this?

281
00:17:44,980 --> 00:17:46,200
But why is that?

282
00:17:46,620 --> 00:17:47,480
How mysterious!

283
00:17:48,160 --> 00:17:50,960
When normally it's pitch black, almost like obsidian!

284
00:17:50,960 --> 00:17:52,460
Who is that?

285
00:17:52,460 --> 00:17:55,360
It's so beautiful, though, isn't it?

286
00:17:55,420 --> 00:17:56,900
Who are you?

287
00:17:58,020 --> 00:17:59,120
Wait, that's right.

288
00:17:59,700 --> 00:18:01,180
This is an inherited memory.

289
00:18:02,020 --> 00:18:06,660
The samurai she's talking about, could it be the swordsman with the earrings I saw?

290
00:18:06,660 --> 00:18:10,320
Does that mean his sword was pitch black, too?

291
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:12,480
Then mine's just like his.

292
00:18:13,320 --> 00:18:15,900
And like his, my own sword just turned red!

293
00:18:16,400 --> 00:18:17,360
It changed color!

294
00:18:17,360 --> 00:18:21,860
Thanks to the power of Nezuko's blood, I have this red blade.

295
00:18:22,580 --> 00:18:28,520
And so, even though it was through a different method, my sword is no different than that swordsman's!

296
00:18:29,300 --> 00:18:33,340
You may think you've gotten stronger, but there are always stronger demons.

297
00:18:34,280 --> 00:18:38,060
I'm only flesh and blood, with a body that's scarred and battered.

298
00:18:39,020 --> 00:18:43,720
And each time I've been on the brink of death, I was saved by someone.

299
00:18:44,840 --> 00:18:47,220
I have to repay what they've done for me!

300
00:18:48,280 --> 00:18:52,860
Everyone who's helped me come as far as I have, has but one wish, one desire!

301
00:18:54,080 --> 00:18:55,520
To defeat the demons!

302
00:18:56,280 --> 00:18:58,140
To protect human lives!

303
00:19:04,600 --> 00:19:06,960
I have to come through for them no matter what!

304
00:19:09,640 --> 00:19:12,500
You're gonna need more than cheap tricks if you want to beat me!

305
00:19:12,500 --> 00:19:16,520
You can slash me all you want, but I'm not gonna feel a thing!

306
00:19:18,280 --> 00:19:20,680
A burning blade, raging sword!

307
00:19:22,040 --> 00:19:23,360
Lord Muzan's memories!

308
00:19:25,200 --> 00:19:28,660
That's the same sword that drove Lord Muzan into a corner!

309
00:19:29,280 --> 00:19:31,140
And nearly beheaded him!

310
00:19:31,140 --> 00:19:37,560
I see that swordsman in him!

311
00:19:42,240 --> 00:19:43,400
Hinokami Kagura!

312
00:19:44,240 --> 00:19:45,420
Son of Halo Dragon!

313
00:19:45,420 --> 00:20:07,280
Kid Dance!

314
00:20:07,280 --> 00:20:30,100
All this time I've been thinking about that one blow.

315
00:20:30,100 --> 00:20:35,600
And the reason that it decapitated Kyutaro back in the entertainment district.

316
00:20:37,280 --> 00:20:44,120
How I felt in that moment, my breathing, the way I exerted myself, the way my body felt

317
00:20:44,120 --> 00:20:46,460
like it was on fire, and my forehead.

318
00:20:48,140 --> 00:20:49,200
Now I know.

319
00:20:49,660 --> 00:20:50,720
I can do it now.

320
00:20:51,940 --> 00:20:53,100
Just one more.

321
00:20:53,540 --> 00:20:55,280
I need to slash all four at once.

322
00:20:56,280 --> 00:20:57,380
Where's the last one?

323
00:21:00,320 --> 00:21:01,960
Kenya, you're okay.

324
00:21:04,160 --> 00:21:05,920
He beheaded the fourth demon.

325
00:21:06,360 --> 00:21:06,960
That's great.

326
00:21:07,280 --> 00:21:07,900
That's great.

327
00:21:08,740 --> 00:21:09,520
But hold on.

328
00:21:09,880 --> 00:21:10,840
Was it simultaneous?

329
00:21:11,800 --> 00:21:12,080
Kenya!

330
00:21:21,600 --> 00:21:22,660
Is that Kenya?

331
00:21:23,300 --> 00:21:25,140
Why does he look like that?

332
00:21:25,140 --> 00:21:27,140
It's like...

333
00:21:28,060 --> 00:21:30,140
It's like...

334
00:21:30,140 --> 00:21:33,740
No one.

335
00:21:33,740 --> 00:21:35,640
No one.

336
00:21:35,760 --> 00:21:36,580
No one.

337
00:21:36,580 --> 00:21:50,600
to live on

338
00:21:50,600 --> 00:22:01,140
are

339
00:22:01,140 --> 00:22:03,180
Oh

340
00:22:03,180 --> 00:22:33,160
Thank you.

341
00:22:33,180 --> 00:23:03,160
Thank you.

342
00:23:03,180 --> 00:23:05,900
Ms. Konroji, how do you go about sheathing that sword?

343
00:23:06,280 --> 00:23:07,960
Oh, uh...

344
00:23:07,960 --> 00:23:09,360
Poison potato!

345
00:23:13,480 --> 00:23:16,680
Oh, come on, I'm just kidding, you guys!

346
00:23:20,180 --> 00:23:21,660
Wow, amazing!

347
00:23:23,960 --> 00:23:26,120
Really? You think it was that amazing?

348
00:23:26,540 --> 00:23:29,740
But of course it is! That's Ms. Konroji for ya!

349
00:23:30,020 --> 00:23:33,880
If you liked it that much, then I guess I can show it to you one more time!

350
00:23:34,680 --> 00:23:39,200
Amazing, Ms. Konroji!

351
00:23:39,460 --> 00:23:40,600
You think so?

352
00:23:41,080 --> 00:23:43,940
Then I guess I have to show you one more time, don't I?

353
00:23:44,020 --> 00:23:45,960
But this one's just for you, Tanjiro!

354
00:23:46,620 --> 00:23:47,820
Wait, first things first!

355
00:23:47,960 --> 00:23:49,060
Next, episode six!

356
00:23:49,060 --> 00:23:50,720
Aren't you going to become a Hashiru?

357
00:23:51,060 --> 00:23:53,020
There! There! There!

358
00:23:53,080 --> 00:23:54,200
Amazing, amazing!

